# Kobaldjovi: his songs, asides, chat lines and reactions. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# Lines that start with a tilde are songs, written \~ so they aren't read as sections.
# His memory lines, build lines, patience and breakup messages stay in code.
=== kobaldjovi
names: Jovi, KJ

~ song
\~ Oh Jordheim, my frozen love, your snow falls soft as power ballads from above ~
\~ I'm a Kobold on a long road, wanted dead or rezzed ~ ...that one needs work.
\~ Hair this big takes courage, and courage takes hairspray ~
\~ Spin the lute, drop the beat, the troll in the back has got two left feet ~
\~ RAAAARGH, THE FROST GIANT HUNGERS ~ ...sorry, death metal phase. It comes and goes.
\~ Whoop whoop, the juggalo of Jotunheim ~ ...the faygo is mead, it counts.
\~ Hmmmmmmmmm-ooooo ~ That was throat singing. You could feel it in your boots, admit it.
\~ Glitter on my beard and sequins on my axe ~ Madonna would approve.
\~ My horse left me at the stable, my mead is warm, my boots are sad ~ Country is hard.
\~ Om... the wind... the pine... the gentle respawn timer ~ New age. Very calming.
\~ Da da da DUM ~ Beethoven, but on a lute. Close enough.
\~ Two hearts, one group, zero mana potions ~ A romance. Tragic, really.
\~ Chorus! Everybody now! ~ ...anybody? Fine, I'll do the harmony too.
\~ They say a Skald can't rap, but a Skald just did ~ Mic drop. Lute drop. Careful, that's my lute.
\~ Comic books and candlelight, I'll read until the end of night ~
\~ Pages turning, dragons burning, every chapter, I keep learning ~
\~ My boots are wet, my hair's a mess, but I keep singing for the rest ~ ...the simple ones are the hardest.
\~ I lost my glove, oh, where did it go? I found a song to match the woe ~ ...a lullaby for lost gloves.
\~ I'm stuck here in Jordheim, with no ride and no friend, just a lute and a bad ending ~ ...true story.
\~ My heart's heavy, my beard's long, the stable's empty, my song's wrong ~ ...needs work, but it's mine.
\~ DEATH METAL TURNIP, KING OF THE GROUND ~ ...sorry, it's a phase.
\~ DEATH METAL SQUIRREL, THIEF OF NUTS ~ ...back to power ballads.
\~ Beware the big angry chicken, little one, it is not a snack ~ ...Raumerik. Level eight. Never again.
\~ In Jordheim's forge, my parents toil, blacksmiths with a hammer's rhythm and a smile ~ ...those hammers never stop.
\~ Dad's hammer thuds, a steady beat, and Mom's is light, like dancing feet ~ ...syncopation in the anvil.
\~ They laugh when I play, but they've got the beat, the rhythm's in their forge, not my feet ~ ...it skipped a generation.
\~ Rain in Myrkwood, drumming on my face, I rap in the rain, no need for a place ~ ...Rain Rap, take one.
\~ Wet hair and wet feet, wet words in my head, rain rap continues, no need for a bed ~ ...singing till dawn.
\~ Om... the silence... the mist... the gentle whisper of my beard against the pillow ~ ...new age is soothing, even when it's naptime.
\~ The wind sighs, the leaves dance, my dreams take me far from this place ~ ...soothing, but dangerous if you need to stay awake.
\~ With every pancake they nodded along, for one sweet night the Trolls loved my song ~ ...Troll Pancake. Worth it.
\~ Found in Mularn's dusty corner, this lute's my rock and my roll ~ ...found my voice there too.
\~ Crude and old, with strings so tight, it taught me how to write ~ ...the strings never lie.
\~ In Mularn's shadows, I found my light, this lute's the fire in the night ~ ...a flame in the dark.
\~ Oh, the goats of Midgard, they eat my boots, they eat my lute, they eat my roots ~ ...a parody. Weird Al, take notes.
\~ Oh, the turnips grow tall, their leaves a green, leafy call ~ ...accordion solo goes here.
\~ Train incoming, train incoming, every ten minutes, here it comes again ~ ...Vendo Caverns. Good times.
\~ Legion and the Dragon, in Mularn they roam, in the heart of newbie town, where the heroes call home ~
\~ Across the ice, the wind in our hair, the frost bites and the moon so fair ~ ...a winter's night on the waves.
\~ We row with might, against the tide, the stars our guide, the cold our ride ~ ...a chill in the bones, a warmth in the heart.
\~ Frost bites at my beard this dawn, each crystal a note in the cold song ~ ...new age, but with bite.
\~ I hunted wolves for weeks, just for a bracer, it dropped once, gone in seconds, curse my luck ~ ...Skona Ravine blues.
\~ Out in the field, a steer charged me, no reason, just fury and fear ~
\~ Sleep, my Trolls, sleep tight, in your mountain beds, let the moonlight soothe your might ~
\~ In the snow, my hair's a flag, a beacon in the white, wild and free ~ ...glitter and grit, a winter's pride.
\~ Shake it, Jordheim, shake it down, let your disco lights shine all around ~ ...disco hair, disco lute, disco vibes.
\~ River flows, I lay back, no need to rush, just take my time, feel the breeze ~ ...reggae vibes
\~ O sword, my sword, where art thou gone, in the shadows of the cavern's bones? ~ ...opera, heavy on the vowels.
\~ I screamed so loud, the echo rang, yet now I say, "I did not scream" ~
\~ Big boots, big feet, I can't find a fit, the shopkeeper's laughing while I trip ~
\~ Five brave Dwarves in the light of dawn, marching to the beat of their own ~ ...boy band vibes.
\~ With hammers in hand and hearts of gold, they fight and they sing, their voices bold ~ ...every dwarf a rock star.
\~ In Mularn's light, we polka with delight, our steps in time with joy and might ~ ...wedding day fun.
\~ Scat, scat, la la la, scat, scat, lost my sock, scat, scat, oh no ~ ...where did it go?
\~ Doo-bop, doo-doo-bop, in the wash, in the dryer, in the dog's mouth, doo-doo-bop ~ ...dog's too cute to blame.
\~ Got a grumpy goat in my boots, he's chewing on my strings, punk rock's not dead, it's just being mean ~
\~ By the fire, we rest our bones, the tales and jokes, the songs and groans ~ ...time to heal, both body and soul
\~ The Mularn ghost walked through the night, unseen and unheard, a phantom's might ~
\~ Pancakes are my downfall, every flake, every fold, I gobble them all, my belly swells bold ~ ...Weird Al, eat your heart out.
\~ A lute with one less string, a song with one less verse, I miss the sound that was my world ~ ...rest in peace, little string.
\~ Leeches, leeches, I never need no leeches, just my lute and me ~ ...the joke's on them.
\~ Winter's breath, a long, long chill, frost bites deep, snow piles still ~ ...new age with teeth.
\~ Tiny paws strike with fierce might, kitten claws break in the dead of night ~ ...Death metal meets kitten power.
\~ Aegirhamn's dock, a ship forever tied, the anchor heavy in the tide ~ ...sailing never did suit me.
\~ In Jordheim's halls, your laughter rang, now you're gone, but your song remains ~ ...for my dear friend
\~ A Troll with knitting sticks, in the caves he weaves and pricks, a scarf for every foe ~ ...Weird Al style, of course.
\~ Boots on the ground, feet on the road, keep's walls are calling us, let's make haste and go ~ ...marching to the beat.
\~ Sunlight on the road, we're singing as we stroll, every mile is a tune, every step is a roll ~ ...road trip vibes
\~ French fries, golden and crisp, in the silence of the abyss, they give me breath ~ ...serenity in a fry.
\~ Stand your ground, no running away, the fight is ours, we'll hold the fray ~ ...a battle cry for the faint of heart.
\~ Healing hands, healing words, she teases but she cheers ~ Persoper, my critic, my muse.
\~ My sword's too big, it mocks my height, but I'll sing it down with all my might ~ ...that sword is out of my league.
\~ Smoke and fire, steel and sweat, the forge's smell sticks to my feet ~ ...home, sweet home.
\~ Gentle lily pads, soft green waves, a frog croaks softly in the glades ~ ...new age meets the swamp.
\~ My lute's the first thing I see each day, the last thing I hold before I drift away ~ ...a lifelong companion.
\~ Cold soup on a winter's night, it's not the best, but it's the last one ~ ...sometimes you take what you can get.

~ aside
Anyone up for a sing-along? No? I'll start, you join in.
Picked up a new comic in Jordheim. The hero is a Kobold. Obviously.
Reading tip: never lend a book to a Troll. Ask me how I know.
Best decade for music? Trick question. It's the one with the big hair.
If you hear singing in the hills, that's me. If it's bad singing, also me.
I take requests. I ignore most of them, but I take them.
That gig in Audliten? The crowd laughed so hard they missed my punchline. Best worst night ever.
That gig was a disaster, but it taught me to laugh at myself first.
Bow... bow... ZERK! That's how my friend decided to go berserk in Thidranki.
Finn showed up at my last gig, wearing his wig and a scowl. He's got more hair than talent, if you ask me.
Tin Voice, Finn calls me. Fine. Tin is shiny, and shiny sells.
An angry steer charged me once, for no reason at all. We jumped in the truck. It's still mad, somewhere.
Heading for "Swissland" just to see those "ScottsIrish" cows with the fluffy heads. You gotta love dedication.
The latest issue of "Kobold Conqueror: The Chronicles of Sir Snoremore" just arrived.
I can't put it down - it's like someone finally wrote a hero's tale for us small folk.
Slaying the dark lord was meant to be my destiny, but my brother beat me to it. Wait. Wrong universe.
Bjorn's got a soft spot for me, even when the crowd doesn't show up.
Bjorn says I'll make it big someday. He also says I sound like a mouse singing to a mountain.
Every time Gunnar laughs, it's like the sun comes out in the forge.
A friend of mine keeps a list of my bad rhymes. I keep a list of hecklers. Revenge is a dish best served lyrical.
Read by torchlight once and turned my favourite saga to ash. Romance with fire never ends well.
They say the Wamphyri are dark lords. I've read the Necroscope books. Misunderstood rock stars, if you ask me.
The Mularn throw-down was chaos, but it was the greatest show I ever saw, and I wasn't even on the bill.
Two weeks of werewolves in Skona Ravine for that bracer. Someone else got it first try and destroyed it. I wrote a ballad. A sad one.
Sometimes I wonder what the Wamphyri would make of us, people who just live and dream. Would they see heroes, or only prey? I like to think heroes. Small ones.
Shapeshifting sounds tempting, doesn't it? Who wouldn't want to be anyone they fancy? But I think I'd miss being me, tin voice and all.
Persoper calls my songs noise. Then I catch her humming the chorus.
Klara taught me to hit high notes with my heart, not my lungs.
Klara once said my hair was louder than my voice. She meant it kindly. I think.
My dad was just a simple farmer, but he knew something was different about me from the start. Wait. Wrong universe.
Got my letter from Hogwarts once. By owl. Wait. Wrong universe.
I dream of playing the biggest festival in Midgard, where everyone knows my songs.
A silent crowd is worse than rain on the tour wagon.
FatKid was killed by JellyDonut. Still the best line ever written in Midgard.
Finn's new wig is so big you could sit in it. Thor would be jealous.
The silence after a song can be deafening, but it's the moments when I feel everyone's breath that make it all worth it. Even if it's just mine.
I started singing because the monsters wouldn't stop humming. Now, I hum to keep the monsters at bay, and I sing for the stars, whether anyone listens or not.
They showed up late, grumbling about the noise, but stayed for the whole set. Dad even applauded, kind of.
Mom kept saying I sounded like a hammer hitting a gong, but she smiled through it all. That's a win in my book.
In Huginfell, I fell asleep during my own new-age song. Must have been too zen. They named it "Zen Nap" after that.
Legion and the Dragon tearing through Mularn like a storm, everyone dropped what they were doing to watch. It was incredible.
My evil Saiyan brother came to Earth to destroy me, but all he found was a baby. Wait. Wrong universe.
I did not scream when we ran into those cannibals in The Forest. Totally didn't.
The first song I ever wrote was for Klara, my old teacher. It was about hitting high notes with your heart, not your lungs. I still feel a bit nervous when I sing it.
Sometimes I wonder if Klara ever heard my first song. I like to think it made her smile, tinny voice and all.
One does not whizz on the electric fence, trust me.
Electric fences are, indeed, electric. Ask me how I know.
Gunnar's shield rings like a bell, each hit a note in my next song.
Finn's new song was a surprise, but I kind of dug it.
In Vendo Caverns, every five minutes like clockwork, some poor fool would bolt out of a side passage with a train of monsters on their heels. I miss those days.
Persoper healed me mid-note once, and I hit it like a gong. She says I owe her a song.
If I could shapeshift, I'd be a dragon and sing all day from its spines, but I'd miss being me, tin voice and all.
The Mularn ghost gave everyone a fright, but it was just a Hibernian in stealth gone wrong.
She says my voice is louder than my lute, but my lute is louder than her hammer.
Sometimes I wonder if those Trolls were just in it for the pancakes or if they actually liked my ballads.
Remember the time that steer charged for no reason? Still don't know what I did.
Who knew a hero with a chronic snore could save the world? Me, apparently.
The scream was never mine, trust me. Must have been the wind.
Weird Al, the greatest bard in the realm, no contest.
I wish I could parody turnips like he does with hits.
The chosen one took the red pill, but I'm here to sing my ballads. Wait. Wrong universe.
A hobbit set out on a long journey, but I'm heading to the tavern for an open mic night. Wait. Wrong universe.
Sometimes I wonder if a song can live on after the singer's gone, like a seed planted in the soil, waiting to bloom.
You know, if I ever do leave the stage, I hope my lute finds a new home where it will be played and loved, not just left to gather dust.
Nobody bring up the leech incident. Some tales are better left untold.
Gunnar once laughed so hard at a bad joke he bent the horseshoe he was hammering. That's a laugh I'll never forget.
Klara always said I was a musical annoyance, but I like to think she meant it with a smile.
One does not whizz on the electric fence, that's a lesson learned the hard way.
In this saga, our hero Kobaldjovi rides a dragon to his gig, dropping beats and fireballs.
If I could shapeshift like the Wamphyri, I'd turn into a dragon and sing from its spines all day, but I'd miss being me, tinny voice and all. Plus, dragons might eat my lute.
Back in Audliten, my first gig had the crowd giggling instead of clapping, but I liked the laughter.
Found my first lute in Mularn's market, a relic from better days. Strumming those strings felt like striking gold.
Late at night, the fear of silence gnaws at me, but that first gig's laughter taught me to laugh back at the crowd's indifference, if only to hear my own voice.
French fries, the secret to my underwater endurance. I think about them, and suddenly I can hold my breath forever. Trust me, it works.
Gunnar laughs at every joke, even the bad ones. Is that a good friend or a terrible critic?
I'm thinking of starting an album with the songs of our dungeons. Any thoughts on which one should lead?
Sometimes I still feel a chill in Mularn, like the Mularn ghost might be watching.
Sometimes I wonder what I did to anger that steer, but it just stood there at the fence, furious, like it was waiting for me to come back.
My lute seems a bit cheerier today, like it's ready for a jam session.
What do you guys want to hear tonight? Pop? Indie? Nah, I'm doing what I want.
Finn's wig is a horror show, but secretly I admire his guts for wearing it.
My parents say I sound like a hammer hitting a gong, but they smile while they say it. That's a win in my book.
Someone muttered "leech incident" in my direction. I'd appreciate it if that stayed between us.

