~ reply grinding
Grinding is just a song with a lot of verses, {0}.
I hum while I hunt, {0}. The monsters hate it. Keeps them off balance.
Grinding's just a song with a heavy beat, {0}. Every mob's a verse.
The monsters line up for the chorus, {0}. It's the Circle of Life, but with teeth.
Every kill's a drumroll, {0}. The tempo picks up, the crowd goes wild.
I'm headbanging and grinding, {0}. Every skull's a snare drum.
The monsters are my backing band, {0}. Every hit's a harmony.
Careful, {0}. I once took on a cockatrice at level eight. Big angry chicken. Bigger mistake.
Turn it up to eleven, {0}. Every hit's a headbang, every kill's a scream.
Every kill's a lyric, {0}. The chorus is the boss fight.
Metallica's coming at me, {0}. Hope you like the drumroll.
I'm facing off with Mozart, {0}. Wish me luck, I might need it.
The monsters might be tuning out, {0}. But my lute never gets tired of the beat.
Humming keeps them on edge, {0}. But maybe I should try a lullaby.
Every kill's a dedication, {0}. The audience loves a personal touch.
The wolves think they can howl for free? Tell them the cover charge is skulls, {0}.
The monsters are learning my tunes, {0}. Maybe they just want to fit in.
Every mob's a tough crowd, {0}, but the loot's like a standing ovation.

~ reply travel
Road trip, {0}? I've got a whole mixtape for the walk.
Wherever it is, {0}, it's closer with a speed song. Allegedly.
Road trip, {0}? I've got enough power ballads to make the horse jealous.
Stablemaster's horse again, {0}? I serenade it every time. It still won't trot in time.
Mularn, {0}? I played there once. Great crowd. Shame about the smell.
Audliten, {0}? That's where I honed my skills, but the crowd was still rough.
